    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nAll modules\n\n### Description\n\nHi Evgeni,\r\n\r\nI've just released a new plugin called `activate.nvim`, it's a plugin installation system for Neovim: https://github.com/roobert/activate.nvim\r\n\r\nI was wondering whether you'd be interested in supporting the idea of an unofficial format for `setup.lua.example` files. I think this could help lower the barrier to entry for many people looking to try Neovim and its various plugins.\r\n\r\nIf you're interested in this idea, I would be happy to open PRs for your various plugins.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to discuss/refine the idea further, you can email me (my github username @gmail.com) or continue this thread.\r\n\r\nKind regards\r\n\r\nRob",
    "closed_at": "2023-09-09T17:29:01Z",
