        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nThat is an interesting plugin, thanks for sharing!\r\n\r\nI'd rather not create these files right away, but it is not a \"no\" indefinitely. I have a couple of thoughts on this, though:\r\n- 'folke/lazy.nvim' already handles `setup()` calls for 'mini.nvim' standalone repositories automatically. There are a couple of modules that require some explicit user configuration for them to be useful ('mini.base16', 'mini.hipatterns'), but the whole point is to have user decide what they want.\r\n    So the only reason I see now for adding 'setup.lua.example' file(s) is to automatically create a file in which users can write their config.\r\n- I'd rather adhere to something like [neovim/packspec](https://github.com/neovim/packspec) if/when it gets properly released.",
